# The goldens are large binaries rewritten in full on every UI change, and every
# refresh would otherwise add the whole set to history, permanently, in every
# clone. LFS is what makes committing them affordable — which is what makes the
# gate reviewable at all: an untracked baseline is only "whatever this machine
# captured last".
#
# This file lives beside Cupertino.xcodeproj rather than at the repo root
# because its patterns are relative to its own directory. Hoisting it up one
# level would silently stop matching, and the next refresh would commit the
# goldens as ordinary blobs with nothing complaining.
#
# Only golden/. source/, appstore/ and website output are regenerated on every
# run and gitignored; the config is text.
Screenshots/golden/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
